here's how Sydney [ __ ] put it when he  was asked what makes a great casting  director there's a coming together of  abilities that raise this job into an  art form  the ability to immediately skip the  expected the cliche the ability to  understand the inner life of a script or  a scene or a moment of behavior between  two people and most of all the ability  to somehow imagine the chemical  reactions possible when the personality  of a specific actor rubs against in an  unexpected way the personality of the  character on the page that is the art of  Lynn Stoll master  here are some of the filmmakers who  relied on Lin's keen eye and  extraordinary instinct for acting talent  Billy Wilder George Stevens Robert waz  Stanley Kramer William Wyler Norman  Jewison how Ashby Blake Edwards John  Cassavetes Mike Nichols and Sydney  [ __ ] and the Academy is honoured  actors from films cast by Lynne with 36  Oscar nominations and 11 Oscar wins on a  more  on a more personal note 34 years ago Lin  heard about my casting work in New York  he hired me and moved me to Los Angeles  to be his associate and he has been my  mentor ever since so many lessons  learned from this glorious man but  mostly Lin taught me by example that  being a success in Hollywood and being a  mensch are not mutually exclusive I love  you Lin I don't know if Oprah Winfrey's  in the house but this is what she would  call a full circle moment on behalf of  my fellow governor's Laura Kennedy and  Bernie Chelsea and the entire casting  directors branch we salute you as a  pioneer we thank you for setting the bar  high and to the first casting director  in the history of the Academy to receive  an Oscar we say congratulations
 

